        "princip_1": {
          "type": "principle",
          "settings": {
            "title": "No polyester",
            "text": "<p>We use natural fibres instead of synthetic ones. Always.<br>No polyester filling hidden on the inside. No synthetic blends disguised as natural materials. And no plastic microfibres shed from synthetic textile fibres.</p>"
          }
        },
        "princip_2": {
          "type": "principle",
          "settings": {
            "title": "No smoke and no mirrors",
            "text": "<p>We don’t hide behind clever wording or carefully selected percentages.<br>No misleading blends. No polyester filling behind a natural cover. No making products sound better than they actually are.<br>What you see is what you get. Including what’s on the inside.</p>"
          }
        },
        "princip_3": {
          "type": "principle",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Price doesn’t call the shots",
            "text": "<p>We believe in fewer, better things. Not more, cheaper ones.<br>We won’t compromise on materials, craftsmanship or fair working conditions to meet a certain price point. Good products should come at a fair price. For everyone involved.</p>"
          }
        },
        "uld": {
          "type": "material",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Wool",
            "what": "<p>Wool is a natural fibre that has been used by humans for thousands of years.<br>Long before synthetic fibres existed, wool was valued for its warmth, durability and ability to adapt to changing temperatures.</p>",
            "why": "<p>Newborn babies are still developing their ability to regulate body temperature. That’s one of the reasons we’re particularly interested in the materials surrounding them.<br>Wool responds to changes in temperature and humidity. It can absorb moisture vapour and release it again, helping create a comfortable environment without trapping moisture against the skin.<br>And because wool is a natural fibre rather than a synthetic one, it doesn’t release plastic microfibres when fibres shed.</p>",
            "where": "<p>We use wool as filling inside LALA the Whale, our Cot Bumper as well as our Bed Bumper.</p>"
          }
        },
        "bomuld": {
          "type": "material",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Cotton",
            "what": "<p>Cotton is a natural plant fibre that has been used to make textiles for thousands of years.<br>The fibres grow around the seeds of the cotton plant and are spun into yarn before being woven or knitted into fabric.</p>",
            "why": "<p>Babies spend a lot of time in direct contact with textiles. That’s why the material against their skin matters to us.<br>Cotton is naturally breathable, soft and absorbent. It allows air to move through the fabric and absorbs moisture, making it a practical choice for bedding and everyday essentials.<br>We only use cotton that is certified to at least OEKO-TEX® STANDARD 100, meaning the textiles have been tested for harmful substances.<br>It can also withstand frequent washing, which is particularly useful when little people are involved.<br>And unlike polyester, cotton doesn’t shed plastic microfibres.</p>",
            "where": "<p>Cotton textiles are used in every LALATOTO product.</p>"
          }
        },
        "kirsebaersten": {
          "type": "material",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Cherry pits",
            "what": "<p>Cherry pits are the hard, natural stones found inside cherries.<br>A byproduct of the fruit industry, they can be cleaned, dried and given a new purpose instead of being discarded.</p>",
            "why": "<p>Some of our products need a little extra weight. But we didn’t want to use plastic pellets.<br>Cherry pits are naturally dense, durable and rounded, making them suitable for weighted inserts.<br>The cherry pits we use are carefully washed without chemicals and dried under controlled conditions.<br>And we particularly like the idea of making use of a material that already exists, rather than producing a synthetic alternative.</p>",
            "where": "<p>Inside the removable weighted insert of Large LALA the Whale and our weighted Bed Bumper.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
